#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0349 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), R2A1HI(Num), A1HI(Num). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 0.85 | 3.5`. Both halves of the pair are declared, so the second conjunct `not var_exists('A1HI')` is FALSE and the rule is silent. The two wildcard patterns are disjoint, so this still yields exactly one expansion (y=1), not two."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col R2A1HI type=Num
col A1HI type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 0.85 | 3.5
